WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.498 --> 00:00:03.831
(opening Netflix theme)

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.537
(calming music)

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:13.050
- At the minute our lesbian TV fix

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.815
is "Gentleman Jack".

00:00:14.815 --> 00:00:15.648
- Gentleman Jack.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.307
- Genkleman.
(laughing)

00:00:17.307 --> 00:00:18.557
Genkleman Jack.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:20.860
- I'm Jess.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.410
- I'm Sophie.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.923
And together we are.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.774
(both laughing)

00:00:26.774 --> 00:00:28.750
- We live in Margate.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.530
- Cute little seaside town.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.860
Been here for about 18
months with my dogs.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.180
- I moved in February.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.460
I came down for Pride last August

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.140
and got absolutely obsessed with it.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.393
And we matched on her.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.740
I'm from Manchester, specifically Bury.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:43.970
Home of the black pudding.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.980
- And I lived in like, a
village south of Leicester.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.350
Which is like, a population of like

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.300
a thousand people or something.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.840
And none of them were gay.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.010
There were actually two lesbians, two.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.471
They were together, obviously.

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:56.233
(both laughing)

00:00:56.233 --> 00:00:57.504
- I think I was really lucky actually,

00:00:57.504 --> 00:00:58.610
growing up in Manchester.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:01.630
Literally walk up and down Canal Street

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.630
thinking I was like, in "Queer As Folk".

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.630
- I spent so long grappling
with my sexuality,

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.560
and I was engaged to a
guy for about five years.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.200
If my boyfriend was out,
I'd just go and like,

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.950
sit on the sofa, put my pajamas on.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.102
And I'd be like, "Oh, it's my time!"

00:01:18.102 --> 00:01:19.410
(both laughing)

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.440
And I would literally
just put "The L Word" on,

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.450
and watch all of it religiously.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.700
Every single episode.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.110
There's Jenny, and she's dating a guy

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.180
and she moves in with him.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:32.090
I think I felt quite a
big connection with Jenny,

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.020
only because I just
related to her so much.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.500
In that first series
where she starts to like,

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.890
dabble in queer culture,
and she just kinda found

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:42.630
this little group that
accepted her for who she was.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.790
And I was like, "That's
what I need to do."

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.620
It really helped to just
normalize my feelings.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.190
Show me that the life
that I wanted for myself

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.430
could still exist if I was gay.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:55.600
- So, do you think I'm
more like Bette than Jenny?

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.680
- You're not like Jenny.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.870
- I just felt like.
- You're quite Shane.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.562
(both laughing)

00:02:01.562 --> 00:02:02.746
(police siren wailing)

00:02:02.746 --> 00:02:04.820
- I would religiously watch "Bad Girls".

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.230
That was like the ultimate like, Top Dog.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.710
I also kinda liked Sylvia, as well.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:12.270
That weird little Nana police woman.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.010
- In what, "Bad Girls"?
- Yeah.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.460
And Shell Dockley, obviously.

00:02:17.131 --> 00:02:18.958
I wouldn't mind being banged up with them.

00:02:18.958 --> 00:02:22.210
(both laughing)

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.899
- Yeah we watched "Orange
Is the New Black".

00:02:23.899 --> 00:02:25.700
That was really good.
- I mean, literally

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.686
rammed full of lesbians,
"Orange Is the New Black".

00:02:27.686 --> 00:02:30.193
(laughing)

00:02:30.193 --> 00:02:31.820
Also I loved "Sugar Rush".

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:35.340
They were more, not my age
'cause I was still quite young.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.660
But, it felt more like,
I could relate to it,

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.190
'cause they were teenagers.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:42.320
And I was like, I could
run away to Brighton.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.030
Maybe that's why I've ended up in Margate.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:48.607
Trying to live my "Sugar
Rush" seaside dreams.

00:02:48.607 --> 00:02:53.607
- "Coronation Street",
Sophie Webster, gay icon.

00:02:54.605 --> 00:02:55.780
(both giggling)

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.830
No, that was, I think
that was 'cause my family

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.530
have always watched "Coronation Street".

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.930
It's something that I even watch now.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.320
Like, oh you hate it.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.680
- Ugh, absolutely sucked.
- But I find,

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.560
I know this is gonna sound really weird,

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.753
but I think "Coronation
Street" grounds me.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.144
We loved "Special",

00:03:10.144 --> 00:03:12.300
we really loved "Special".
- "Special" was so pure.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.240
- We devoured that.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.780
- It wasn't just about him being gay.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.200
- No.
- That wasn't the main

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.830
like, crux of the show.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:20.950
Which I think is quite rare.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.510
Like, it was just about
him as a character.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.860
- It was quite a brave show, really.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.990
'Cause it was, I mean.
- Yeah.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:29.350
- It showed disability and he
never let it hold him back.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.820
It was really nice and
really well-represented.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:32.930
- I think that's one of the best shows

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.000
that I've watched recently.
- Yeah.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.790
It's really reassuring to see

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.130
queer characters living normally.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.640
That's what I think we need more of.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.810
Because the representation
is mainly of sex.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:46.140
Like, "Blue Is the Warmest
Color" for instance.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.920
I loved that film.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.660
But the only thing people were talking

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:50.760
about in it was the sex.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.720
That's what it always focuses on in TV

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:53.740
and film and everything.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.540
Apart from "The L Word"
and things like that.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.485
But that still was super over-sexualized,

00:03:57.485 --> 00:03:59.340
I thought in some parts.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.204
- That's why we loved it,

00:04:00.204 --> 00:04:02.680
obviously.
- Yeah, obviously.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.560
- Kind of a bit obsessed
with Clare Balding.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.500
Probably the most famous
lesbian TV presenter.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.940
- For Jess' 30th Birthday,
we had a huge party.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.830
I turned up with a
lifesize cardboard cutout

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:16.900
of Clare Balding.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.550
Someone else turned up with
loads of Clare Balding masks.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:20.720
We didn't really know
what to do with them,

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.230
so we put them in the spare bedroom.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.630
- In the window, like facing outwards.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.197
And the neighbor came 'round and said,

00:04:26.197 --> 00:04:28.256
"Can you take the cutout of Princess Diana

00:04:28.256 --> 00:04:30.144
"out of your window?
(laughing)

00:04:30.144 --> 00:04:32.300
"It's really freaking my wife out."

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.840
We were like, "What?

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.880
Oh, Clare."

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.380
(laughing)
- Oh, Clare, yeah.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:43.890
TV, film, can have such a
bigger impact on gay people.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:45.960
Everything's made for
heterosexual couples.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.210
It's so inbred in our culture,

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.380
that when you're gay
you have to kinda reach

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:51.213
for something else.

00:04:51.213 --> 00:04:52.550
So, I think when you see it on TV,

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:54.680
it is much more powerful for gay people.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.630
It just gives you a sense of belonging.

00:04:58.221 --> 00:05:00.888
(calming music)

